Package: mia-retext
Version: 8.1.0-mia2
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, libegl1, libgl1, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, libdbus-1-3, libglib2.0-0, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libxcb1, libxcb-cursor0, libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-image0, libxcb-keysyms1, libxcb-randr0, libxcb-render-util0, libxcb-shape0, libxcb-xinerama0, libxcb-xkb1
Recommends: libenchant-2-2
Provides: retext
Conflicts: retext
Replaces: retext
Maintainer: Miadi <mia@jgwill.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/miadisabelle/mia-retext
Description: ReText, Markdown and reStructuredText editor, from the miadisabelle fork
 The ReText of github.com/miadisabelle/mia-retext, in place of the
 distribution's retext package (Ubuntu 22.04 ships 7.2.3 on PyQt5).
 /usr/bin/retext runs it from its own venv, /usr/lib/mia-retext/venv,
 built at install from the wheels this package carries: PyQt6, Markups,
 Markdown, docutils, Pygments, pyenchant and chardet, never from PyPI and
 never the distribution's. A new python3 rebuilds the venv.
 .
 Spell checking needs libenchant-2-2 and a dictionary. The WebEngine
 preview is not included.
